IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc15-special.l4 -- sections 476 to 477.4 of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46 (Part XIV, Jurisdiction, "Special Jurisdiction"):
-- where an offence is deemed to have been committed (s 476), and offences outside Canada: the definition of ship (s 477), the offences deemed
-- committed in Canada (s 477.1), the consent of the Attorney General of Canada (s 477.2), powers of arrest, entry, search and seizure (s 477.3) and
-- certificates (s 477.4). Layer 1: the law, objectively, from the text alone. Imports the core only (`ccc-core`) and `daydate`.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30).
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- How a result reads: see the head of ccc15-general.l4 and NOTES.md ("Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (ccc15)"):
-- JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words); NOTHING (not covered). A caller must never turn NOTHING into JUST FALSE.

§ `Section 476 -- Special jurisdictions`

-- 476 is a deeming rule with five paragraphs. Each paragraph is a function of (the circumstances of the offence, how the territorial division is connected to it);
-- the section's own answer gathers them. A paragraph whose circumstances are not those of the case says no ("where ..." unmet: JUST FALSE); a paragraph whose circumstances
-- are those of the case but names other territorial divisions says nothing about this one (NOTHING: the deeming is limited by the divisions it names).
-- src:8583 | Special jurisdictions
-- src:8584 | 476 For the purposes of this Act,
-- src:8585 | (a) where an offence is committed in or on any water or on a bridge between two or more territorial divisions, the offence shall be deemed to have been committed in any of the territorial divisions;
-- src:8586 | (b) where an offence is committed on the boundary of two or more territorial divisions or within five hundred metres of any such boundary, or the offence was commenced within one territorial division and completed within another, the offence shall be deemed to have been committed in any of the territorial divisions;
-- src:8587 | (c) where an offence is committed in or on a vehicle employed in a journey, or on board a vessel employed on a navigable river, canal or inland water, the offence shall be deemed to have been committed in any territorial division through which the vehicle or vessel passed in the course of the journey or voyage on which the offence was committed, and where the center or other part of the road, or navigable river, canal or inland water on which the vehicle or vessel passed in the course of the journey or voyage is the boundary of two or more territorial divisions, the offence shall be deemed to have been committed in any of the territorial divisions;
-- src:8588 | (d) where an offence is committed in an aircraft in the course of a flight of that aircraft, it shall be deemed to have been committed
-- src:8589 | (i) in the territorial division in which the flight commenced,
-- src:8590 | (ii) in any territorial division over which the aircraft passed in the course of the flight, or
-- src:8591 | (iii) in the territorial division in which the flight ended; and
-- src:8592 | (e) where an offence is committed in respect of the mail in the course of its door-to-door delivery, the offence shall be deemed to have been committed in any territorial division through which the mail was carried on that delivery.
@ref s 476 (src:8583-8592)
DECLARE `s 476 circumstances of the offence` HAS
    `committed in or on any water or on a bridge between two or more territorial divisions`   IS A BOOLEAN   -- (a)
    `metres between the place of the offence and the boundary of two or more territorial divisions`   IS A MAYBE NUMBER   -- (b): JUST 0 on the boundary; NOTHING when there is no such boundary nearby
    `commenced within one territorial division and completed within another`   IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)
    `committed in or on a vehicle employed in a journey, or on board a vessel employed on a navigable river, canal or inland water`   IS A BOOLEAN   -- (c)
    `the center or other part of the road, or navigable river, canal or inland water on which the vehicle or vessel passed in the course of the journey or voyage is the boundary of two or more territorial divisions`   IS A BOOLEAN   -- (c)
    `committed in an aircraft in the course of a flight of that aircraft`   IS A BOOLEAN   -- (d)
    `committed in respect of the mail in the course of its door-to-door delivery`   IS A BOOLEAN   -- (e)

@ref s 476 (src:8583-8592)
DECLARE `s 476 how the territorial division is connected to the offence` HAS
    `it is one of the territorial divisions between which the water or the bridge lies`   IS A BOOLEAN   -- (a)
    `it is one of the territorial divisions of the boundary on or within five hundred metres of which the offence was committed`   IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)
    `it is the territorial division within which the offence was commenced or the one within which it was completed`   IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)
    `it is a territorial division through which the vehicle or vessel passed in the course of the journey or voyage on which the offence was committed`   IS A BOOLEAN   -- (c)
    `it is one of the territorial divisions of which the center or other part of the road, or navigable river, canal or inland water is the boundary`   IS A BOOLEAN   -- (c)
    `it is the territorial division in which the flight commenced`   IS A BOOLEAN   -- (d)(i)
    `it is a territorial division over which the aircraft passed in the course of the flight`   IS A BOOLEAN   -- (d)(ii)
    `it is the territorial division in which the flight ended`   IS A BOOLEAN   -- (d)(iii)
    `it is a territorial division through which the mail was carried on that delivery`   IS A BOOLEAN   -- (e)

