-- The section's own answer: JUST TRUE when any paragraph deems the offence committed in the division; otherwise NOTHING when some paragraph's circumstances are those of the case
-- but the division is not one it names; otherwise JUST FALSE (no paragraph applies).
@ref s 476 (src:8583-8592)
GIVEN circumstances IS A `s 476 circumstances of the offence`
      link IS A `s 476 how the territorial division is connected to the offence`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 476 the offence is deemed to have been committed in the territorial division` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF    `paragraph (a)` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `paragraph (b), boundary` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `paragraph (b), commenced and completed` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           OR `paragraph (c), journey` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `paragraph (c), boundary road or water` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `paragraph (d)` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `paragraph (e)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           THEN JUST TRUE
        IF    `paragraph (a)` EQUALS NOTHING OR `paragraph (b), boundary` EQUALS NOTHING OR `paragraph (b), commenced and completed` EQUALS NOTHING
           OR `paragraph (c), journey` EQUALS NOTHING OR `paragraph (c), boundary road or water` EQUALS NOTHING OR `paragraph (d)` EQUALS NOTHING OR `paragraph (e)` EQUALS NOTHING
           THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the offence shall be deemed to have been committed in any of the territorial divisions" (the paragraph that applies names other divisions)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where an offence is committed" (no paragraph of section 476 applies)
    WHERE
        `paragraph (a)` MEANS `s 476(a) the offence is deemed to have been committed in the territorial division` circumstances link
        `paragraph (b), boundary` MEANS `s 476(b) the offence is deemed to have been committed in the territorial division, the offence being committed on or within five hundred metres of the boundary` circumstances link
        `paragraph (b), commenced and completed` MEANS `s 476(b) the offence is deemed to have been committed in the territorial division, the offence being commenced within one territorial division and completed within another` circumstances link
        `paragraph (c), journey` MEANS `s 476(c) the offence is deemed to have been committed in the territorial division, the offence being committed in or on a vehicle or on board a vessel` circumstances link
        `paragraph (c), boundary road or water` MEANS `s 476(c) the offence is deemed to have been committed in the territorial division, the road or water on which the vehicle or vessel passed being the boundary of two or more territorial divisions` circumstances link
        `paragraph (d)` MEANS `s 476(d) the offence is deemed to have been committed in the territorial division, the offence being committed in an aircraft in the course of a flight` circumstances link
        `paragraph (e)` MEANS `s 476(e) the offence is deemed to have been committed in the territorial division, the offence being committed in respect of the mail` circumstances link

§ `Section 477 -- Definition of ship; saving`

-- 477 (1) is a definition ("ship includes ..."), scoped by its own words "In sections 477.1 to 477.4". The provision in which the word is used is a Provision of the Code;
-- sections are decimals, so 477.1 to 477.4 is a range test. A list that "includes" is not closed: a case outside it is NOT COVERED.
-- "without regard to method or lack of propulsion" makes propulsion irrelevant, so no input stands for it.
-- src:8593 | Definition of ship
-- src:8594 | 477 (1) In sections 477.1 to 477.4, ship includes any description of vessel, boat or craft designed, used or capable of being used solely or partly for marine navigation, without regard to method or lack of propulsion.
@ref s 477(1) (src:8593-8594)
GIVEN `the provision in which the word ship is used` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `it is a vessel, boat or craft` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is designed, used or capable of being used solely or partly for marine navigation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 477(1) ship` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the provision in which the word ship is used`'s `section` LESS THAN 477.1 OR `the provision in which the word ship is used`'s `section` GREATER THAN 477.4 THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In sections 477.1 to 477.4"
        IF `it is a vessel, boat or craft` AND `it is designed, used or capable of being used solely or partly for marine navigation` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "ship includes any description of vessel, boat or craft"

-- 477 (2) Saving: nothing in sections 477.1 to 477.4 limits the operation of any other Act of Parliament or the jurisdiction a court may exercise apart from those sections.
-- The function asks whether they limit; the text says they do not (a flat negative), so JUST FALSE is the text's own answer.
-- src:8595 | Saving
-- src:8596 | (2) Nothing in sections 477.1 to 477.4 limits the operation of any other Act of Parliament or the jurisdiction that a court may exercise apart from those sections.
@ref s 477(2) (src:8595-8596)
DECLARE `s 477(2) what is said to be limited` IS ONE OF
    `s 477(2) the operation of another Act of Parliament`
    `s 477(2) the jurisdiction that a court may exercise apart from sections 477.1 to 477.4`
    `s 477(2) something else`

@ref s 477(2) (src:8595-8596)
GIVEN `the section said to limit it` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `what is said to be limited` IS A `s 477(2) what is said to be limited`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 477(2) the section limits the operation of any other Act of Parliament or the jurisdiction that a court may exercise apart from sections 477.1 to 477.4` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the section said to limit it`'s `section` LESS THAN 477.1 OR `the section said to limit it`'s `section` GREATER THAN 477.4 THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Nothing in sections 477.1 to 477.4"
        IF `what is said to be limited` EQUALS `s 477(2) something else` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any other Act of Parliament or the jurisdiction that a court may exercise apart from those sections"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in sections 477.1 to 477.4 limits the operation of any other Act of Parliament or the jurisdiction that a court may exercise apart from those sections"

§ `Section 477.1 -- Offences outside of Canada`

-- 477.1 deems an act or omission that would be an offence under a federal law if it occurred in Canada to have been committed in Canada, if it falls within (a) to (e).
-- "Federal law" (section 2 of the Oceans Act), "permanent resident" (subsection 2(1) of the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act) and the Oceans Act's marine installation are terms of other Acts:
-- asked as plain facts. "Ship" is as section 477(1) defines it: an input (the answer of `s 477(1) ship`).
-- src:8597 | Offences outside of Canada
-- src:8598 | 477.1 Every person who commits an act or omission that, if it occurred in Canada, would be an offence under a federal law, within the meaning of section 2 of the Oceans Act, is deemed to have committed that act or omission in Canada if it is an act or omission
-- src:8599 | (a) in the exclusive economic zone of Canada that
-- src:8600 | (i) is committed by a person who is in the exclusive economic zone of Canada in connection with exploring or exploiting, conserving or managing the natural resources, whether living or non-living, of the exclusive economic zone of Canada, and
-- src:8601 | (ii) is committed by or in relation to a person who is a Canadian citizen or a permanent resident within the meaning of subsection 2(1) of the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act;
-- src:8602 | (b) that is committed in a place in or above the continental shelf of Canada and that is an offence in that place by virtue of section 20 of the Oceans Act;
-- src:8603 | (c) that is committed outside Canada on board or by means of a ship registered or licensed, or for which an identification number has been issued, pursuant to any Act of Parliament;
-- src:8604 | (d) that is committed outside Canada in the course of hot pursuit; or
-- src:8605 | (e) that is committed outside the territory of any state by a Canadian citizen.
@ref s 477.1 (src:8597-8605)
DECLARE `s 477.1 facts of the act or omission` HAS
    `it would, if it occurred in Canada, be an offence under a federal law, within the meaning of section 2 of the Oceans Act`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is in the exclusive economic zone of Canada`   IS A BOOLEAN   -- (a)
    `it is committed by a person who is in the exclusive economic zone of Canada in connection with exploring or exploiting, conserving or managing the natural resources, whether living or non-living, of the exclusive economic zone of Canada`   IS A BOOLEAN   -- (a)(i)
    `it is committed by or in relation to a person who is a Canadian citizen or a permanent resident within the meaning of subsection 2(1) of the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act`   IS A BOOLEAN   -- (a)(ii)
    `it is committed in a place in or above the continental shelf of Canada and is an offence in that place by virtue of section 20 of the Oceans Act`   IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)
    `it is committed outside Canada on board or by means of a ship`   IS A BOOLEAN   -- (c)
    `the ship is registered or licensed, or has had an identification number issued, pursuant to an Act of Parliament`   IS A BOOLEAN   -- (c)
    `it is committed outside Canada in the course of hot pursuit`   IS A BOOLEAN   -- (d)
    `it is committed outside the territory of any state by a Canadian citizen`   IS A BOOLEAN   -- (e)

@ref s 477.1 (src:8597-8605)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 477.1 facts of the act or omission`
      `the vessel is a ship, by s 477(1) ship` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 477.1 the person is deemed to have committed the act or omission in Canada` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT facts's `it would, if it occurred in Canada, be an offence under a federal law, within the meaning of section 2 of the Oceans Act` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every person who commits an act or omission that, if it occurred in Canada, would be an offence under a federal law"
        IF `paragraph (a)` OR facts's `it is committed in a place in or above the continental shelf of Canada and is an offence in that place by virtue of section 20 of the Oceans Act` OR facts's `it is committed outside Canada in the course of hot pursuit` OR facts's `it is committed outside the territory of any state by a Canadian citizen` THEN JUST TRUE   -- (a), (b), (d) and (e)
        IF `paragraph (c) but for the meaning of ship` AND `the vessel is a ship, by s 477(1) ship` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE   -- (c)
        IF `paragraph (c) but for the meaning of ship` AND `the vessel is a ship, by s 477(1) ship` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the vessel is a ship is for section 477(1), which says "includes", and is not determined
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is deemed to have committed that act or omission in Canada if it is an act or omission" (none of (a) to (e) holds: a failed "if", fork: if-on-deeming)
    WHERE
        `paragraph (a)` MEANS
                facts's `it is in the exclusive economic zone of Canada`
            AND facts's `it is committed by a person who is in the exclusive economic zone of Canada in connection with exploring or exploiting, conserving or managing the natural resources, whether living or non-living, of the exclusive economic zone of Canada`
            AND facts's `it is committed by or in relation to a person who is a Canadian citizen or a permanent resident within the meaning of subsection 2(1) of the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act`
        `paragraph (c) but for the meaning of ship` MEANS
                facts's `it is committed outside Canada on board or by means of a ship`
            AND facts's `the ship is registered or licensed, or has had an identification number issued, pursuant to an Act of Parliament`

§ `Section 477.2 -- Consent of Attorney General of Canada`

-- The eight days of section 477.2: "not later than eight days after the proceedings are commenced". The consent is in time when it is obtained on or before the eighth day after
-- the day the proceedings are commenced (fork: eight-days-inclusive). When no consent has been obtained, the question is asked as at a date (fork: as-at-date): the consent is out of time
-- once the as-at date is more than eight days after the day the proceedings were commenced. Dates are day counts (`Day`), so months and leap years are the calendar's.
-- src:8606 | Consent of Attorney General of Canada
-- src:8607 | 477.2 (1) No proceedings in respect of an offence committed in or on the territorial sea of Canada shall be continued unless the consent of the Attorney General of Canada is obtained not later than eight days after the proceedings are commenced, if the accused is not a Canadian citizen and the offence is alleged to have been committed on board any ship registered outside Canada.
@ref s 477.2(1) (src:8606-8607)
GIVEN `the date on which the proceedings were commenced` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the consent of the Attorney General of Canada was obtained` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date as at which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 477.2 the consent was not obtained not later than eight days after the proceedings were commenced` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date on which the consent of the Attorney General of Canada was obtained`
    WHEN JUST obtained THEN (Day obtained MINUS Day `the date on which the proceedings were commenced`) GREATER THAN 8
    WHEN NOTHING THEN (Day `the date as at which the question is asked` MINUS Day `the date on which the proceedings were commenced`) GREATER THAN 8

@ref s 477.2(1) (src:8606-8607)
GIVEN `the date on which the proceedings were commenced` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 477.2 the last day on which the consent of the Attorney General of Canada may be obtained` MEANS
    Date (DATE_DAY `the date on which the proceedings were commenced` PLUS 8) (DATE_MONTH `the date on which the proceedings were commenced`) (DATE_YEAR `the date on which the proceedings were commenced`)

-- (1) is titled as the bar: JUST TRUE means the proceedings shall not be continued. "No proceedings ... shall be continued unless the consent ... is obtained not later than eight days
-- after the proceedings are commenced, if the accused is not a Canadian citizen and the offence is alleged to have been committed on board any ship registered outside Canada."
-- Inside the eight days with no consent yet, the bar has not yet bitten: JUST FALSE (the consent can still be obtained; the date to watch is the answer of `s 477.2 the last day ...`).
@ref s 477.2(1) (src:8606-8607)
GIVEN `the offence is committed in or on the territorial sea of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused is a Canadian citizen` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence is alleged to have been committed on board a ship registered outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are by way of` IS A `Mode of proceeding`
      `the date on which the proceedings were commenced` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the consent of the Attorney General of Canada was obtained` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date as at which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 477.2(1) the proceedings are barred from being continued for want of the consent of the Attorney General of Canada` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 477.2(1.1) subsection (1) does not apply to the proceedings` `the proceedings are by way of` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not apply to proceedings by way of summary conviction"
        IF NOT `the offence is committed in or on the territorial sea of Canada` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No proceedings in respect of an offence committed in or on the territorial sea of Canada"
        IF `the accused is a Canadian citizen` OR NOT `the offence is alleged to have been committed on board a ship registered outside Canada` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the accused is not a Canadian citizen and the offence is alleged to have been committed on board any ship registered outside Canada"
        IF `s 477.2 the consent was not obtained not later than eight days after the proceedings were commenced` `the date on which the proceedings were commenced` `the date on which the consent of the Attorney General of Canada was obtained` `the date as at which the question is asked` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the consent of the Attorney General of Canada is obtained not later than eight days after the proceedings are commenced"

-- (1.1) is a flat negative: JUST TRUE says that subsection (1) does not apply.
-- src:8608 | Exception
-- src:8609 | (1.1) Subsection (1) does not apply to proceedings by way of summary conviction.
@ref s 477.2(1.1) (src:8608-8609)
GIVEN `the proceedings are by way of` IS A `Mode of proceeding`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 477.2(1.1) subsection (1) does not apply to the proceedings` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are by way of` EQUALS `on summary conviction`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "does not apply to proceedings by way of summary conviction" (the text says nothing of proceedings by indictment)

-- (2) The same bar for proceedings in which the courts have jurisdiction by virtue only of paragraph 477.1(a) or (b). Subsection (1.1) speaks of "subsection (1)" only.
-- Whether the courts have jurisdiction by virtue only of those paragraphs is a plain fact (it turns on the answer of s 477.1 and on the absence of any other basis of jurisdiction).
-- src:8610 | Consent of Attorney General of Canada
-- src:8611 | (2) No proceedings in respect of which courts have jurisdiction by virtue only of paragraph 477.1(a) or (b) shall be continued unless the consent of the Attorney General of Canada is obtained not later than eight days after the proceedings are commenced, if the accused is not a Canadian citizen and the offence is alleged to have been committed on board any ship registered outside Canada.
@ref s 477.2(2) (src:8610-8611)
GIVEN `the courts have jurisdiction by virtue only of paragraph 477.1(a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused is a Canadian citizen` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence is alleged to have been committed on board a ship registered outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the proceedings were commenced` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the consent of the Attorney General of Canada was obtained` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date as at which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 477.2(2) the proceedings are barred from being continued for want of the consent of the Attorney General of Canada` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the courts have jurisdiction by virtue only of paragraph 477.1(a) or (b)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No proceedings in respect of which courts have jurisdiction by virtue only of paragraph 477.1(a) or (b)"
        IF `the accused is a Canadian citizen` OR NOT `the offence is alleged to have been committed on board a ship registered outside Canada` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the accused is not a Canadian citizen and the offence is alleged to have been committed on board any ship registered outside Canada"
        IF `s 477.2 the consent was not obtained not later than eight days after the proceedings were commenced` `the date on which the proceedings were commenced` `the date on which the consent of the Attorney General of Canada was obtained` `the date as at which the question is asked` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the consent of the Attorney General of Canada is obtained not later than eight days after the proceedings are commenced"

-- (3) The same bar, with no condition on the accused or the ship, for proceedings in which the courts have jurisdiction by virtue only of paragraph 477.1(d) or (e).
-- src:8612 | Consent of Attorney General of Canada
-- src:8613 | (3) No proceedings in respect of which courts have jurisdiction by virtue only of paragraph 477.1(d) or (e) shall be continued unless the consent of the Attorney General of Canada is obtained not later than eight days after the proceedings are commenced.
@ref s 477.2(3) (src:8612-8613)
GIVEN `the courts have jurisdiction by virtue only of paragraph 477.1(d) or (e)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the proceedings were commenced` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the consent of the Attorney General of Canada was obtained` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date as at which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 477.2(3) the proceedings are barred from being continued for want of the consent of the Attorney General of Canada` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the courts have jurisdiction by virtue only of paragraph 477.1(d) or (e)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No proceedings in respect of which courts have jurisdiction by virtue only of paragraph 477.1(d) or (e)"
        IF `s 477.2 the consent was not obtained not later than eight days after the proceedings were commenced` `the date on which the proceedings were commenced` `the date on which the consent of the Attorney General of Canada was obtained` `the date as at which the question is asked` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the consent of the Attorney General of Canada is obtained not later than eight days after the proceedings are commenced"

-- (4) The text names no party who must file the consent: no actor is invented (fork: bare-must),
-- so this is a decision function. JUST TRUE means the requirement is met; JUST FALSE means it is not (a "must" not done: fork: bare-must).
-- src:8614 | Consent to be filed
-- src:8615 | (4) The consent of the Attorney General required by subsection (1), (2) or (3) must be filed with the clerk of the court in which the proceedings have been instituted.
@ref s 477.2(4) (src:8614-8615)
GIVEN `a consent of the Attorney General is required by subsection (1), (2) or (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the consent has been filed with the clerk of the court in which the proceedings have been instituted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 477.2(4) the consent has been filed as the subsection requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `a consent of the Attorney General is required by subsection (1), (2) or (3)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The consent of the Attorney General required by subsection (1), (2) or (3)"
        IF `the consent has been filed with the clerk of the court in which the proceedings have been instituted` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be filed with the clerk of the court in which the proceedings have been instituted" (a "must" not done)

§ `Section 477.3 -- Exercising powers of arrest, entry, etc.`

-- "In the circumstances referred to in that section" is the answer of `s 477.1 the person is deemed to have committed the act or omission in Canada`: an input.
-- src:8616 | Exercising powers of arrest, entry, etc.
-- src:8617 | 477.3 (1) Every power of arrest, entry, search or seizure or other power that could be exercised in Canada in respect of an act or omission referred to in section 477.1 may be exercised, in the circumstances referred to in that section,
-- src:8618 | (a) at the place or on board the ship or marine installation or structure, within the meaning of section 2 of the Oceans Act, where the act or omission occurred; or
-- src:8619 | (b) where hot pursuit has been commenced, at any place on the seas, other than a place that is part of the territorial sea of any other state.
@ref s 477.3(1) (src:8616-8619)
DECLARE `s 477.3(1) the place where the power is to be exercised` IS ONE OF
    `s 477.3(1)(a) the place where the act or omission occurred`
    `s 477.3(1)(a) on board the ship or marine installation or structure where the act or omission occurred`
    `s 477.3(1)(b) a place on the seas that is not part of the territorial sea of any other state`
    `s 477.3(1)(b) a place on the seas that is part of the territorial sea of any other state`
    `s 477.3(1) another place`

@ref s 477.3(1) (src:8616-8619)
GIVEN `the power is a power of arrest, entry, search or seizure or other power that could be exercised in Canada in respect of the act or omission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act or omission is one referred to in section 477.1, in the circumstances referred to in that section, by s 477.1` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `hot pursuit has been commenced` IS A BOOLEAN
      place IS A `s 477.3(1) the place where the power is to be exercised`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 477.3(1) the power may be exercised at the place` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the power is a power of arrest, entry, search or seizure or other power that could be exercised in Canada in respect of the act or omission` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every power of arrest, entry, search or seizure or other power that could be exercised in Canada in respect of an act or omission referred to in section 477.1"
        IF `the act or omission is one referred to in section 477.1, in the circumstances referred to in that section, by s 477.1` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the circumstances are those referred to in section 477.1 is for that section and is not determined
        IF `the act or omission is one referred to in section 477.1, in the circumstances referred to in that section, by s 477.1` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the circumstances referred to in that section"
        IF place EQUALS `s 477.3(1)(a) the place where the act or omission occurred` THEN JUST TRUE   -- (a)
        IF place EQUALS `s 477.3(1)(a) on board the ship or marine installation or structure where the act or omission occurred` THEN JUST TRUE   -- (a)
        IF place EQUALS `s 477.3(1)(b) a place on the seas that is not part of the territorial sea of any other state`
            THEN IF `hot pursuit has been commenced`
                 THEN JUST TRUE   -- (b)
                 ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where hot pursuit has been commenced, at any place on the seas"
        IF place EQUALS `s 477.3(1)(b) a place on the seas that is part of the territorial sea of any other state`
            THEN IF `hot pursuit has been commenced`
                 THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "other than a place that is part of the territorial sea of any other state" (fork: other-than)
                 ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where hot pursuit has been commenced, at any place on the seas"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "(a) at the place or on board the ship or marine installation or structure, within the meaning of section 2 of the Oceans Act, where the act or omission occurred; or (b) where hot pursuit has been commenced" name two kinds of place and do not say "only"

-- src:8620 | Arrest, search, seizure, etc.
-- src:8621 | (2) A justice or judge in any territorial division in Canada has jurisdiction to authorize an arrest, entry, search or seizure or an investigation or other ancillary matter related to an offence
-- src:8622 | (a) committed in or on the territorial sea of Canada or any area of the sea that forms part of the internal waters of Canada, or
-- src:8623 | (b) referred to in section 477.1
-- src:8624 | in the same manner as if the offence had been committed in that territorial division.
@ref s 477.3(2) (src:8620-8624)
GIVEN `s 2 justice: the person is a justice or judge` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the matter is an arrest, entry, search or seizure or an investigation or other ancillary matter related to the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence is committed in or on the territorial sea of Canada or any area of the sea that forms part of the internal waters of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence is one referred to in section 477.1, by s 477.1` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 477.3(2) a justice or judge in any territorial division in Canada has jurisdiction to authorize the matter` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`s 2 justice: the person is a justice or judge` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A justice or judge in any territorial division in Canada has jurisdiction"
        IF NOT `the matter is an arrest, entry, search or seizure or an investigation or other ancillary matter related to the offence` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an arrest, entry, search or seizure or an investigation or other ancillary matter related to an offence"
        IF `the offence is committed in or on the territorial sea of Canada or any area of the sea that forms part of the internal waters of Canada` THEN JUST TRUE   -- (a)
        IF `the offence is one referred to in section 477.1, by s 477.1` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE   -- (b)
        IF `the offence is one referred to in section 477.1, by s 477.1` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the offence is referred to in section 477.1 is for that section and is not determined
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "(a) committed in or on the territorial sea of Canada or any area of the sea that forms part of the internal waters of Canada, or" and "(b) referred to in section 477.1" name two kinds of offence and do not say "only"

-- (3) Limitation. Titled as the bar: JUST TRUE means the powers shall not be exercised outside Canada. A prohibition limited by "without the consent of the Attorney General of Canada":
-- with the consent the case falls outside the limit and the text says nothing more (NOTHING), the brief's rule for a prohibition limited by its own wording.
-- src:8625 | Limitation
-- src:8626 | (3) Where an act or omission that is an offence by virtue only of section 477.1 is alleged to have been committed on board any ship registered outside Canada, the powers referred to in subsection (1) shall not be exercised outside Canada with respect to that act or omission without the consent of the Attorney General of Canada.
@ref s 477.3(3) (src:8625-8626)
GIVEN `the act or omission is an offence by virtue only of section 477.1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act or omission is alleged to have been committed on board a ship registered outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the powers are to be exercised outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Attorney General of Canada has consented` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 477.3(3) the powers are barred from being exercised outside Canada without the consent of the Attorney General of Canada` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the act or omission is an offence by virtue only of section 477.1` AND `the act or omission is alleged to have been committed on board a ship registered outside Canada`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an act or omission that is an offence by virtue only of section 477.1 is alleged to have been committed on board any ship registered outside Canada" (a failed "where")
        IF NOT `the powers are to be exercised outside Canada` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "shall not be exercised outside Canada"
        IF `the Attorney General of Canada has consented` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "without the consent of the Attorney General of Canada" (fork: without-consent)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 477.4 -- Evidence`

-- 477.4 (1) and (2) [Repealed, 1996, c. 31, s. 71]. No operative text: carried as a quotation.
-- src:8627 | 477.4 (1) and (2) [Repealed, 1996, c. 31, s. 71]
@ref s 477.4(1) and (2), repealed (src:8627)
`s 477.4(1) and (2) as the text shows them` MEANS "477.4 (1) and (2) [Repealed, 1996, c. 31, s. 71]"

-- The last words of (b) can be read two ways (fork: certificate-statement): (A, taken) the statement is that the location was in an area of a fishing zone of Canada that is not within the internal waters or the
-- territorial sea, or that it was outside the territory of any state; (B) "not within" governs all three places. A certificate under subsection 23(1) of the Oceans Act is a plain fact.
-- src:8628 | Evidence
-- src:8629 | (3) In proceedings in respect of an offence,
-- src:8630 | (a) a certificate referred to in subsection 23(1) of the Oceans Act, or
-- src:8631 | (b) a certificate issued by or under the authority of the Minister of Foreign Affairs containing a statement that any geographical location specified in the certificate was, at any time material to the proceedings, in an area of a fishing zone of Canada that is not within the internal waters of Canada or the territorial sea of Canada or outside the territory of any state,
-- src:8632 | is conclusive proof of the truth of the statement without proof of the signature or official character of the person appearing to have issued the certificate.
@ref s 477.4(3) (src:8628-8632)
DECLARE `s 477.4(3) the kind of certificate` IS ONE OF
    `s 477.4(3)(a) a certificate referred to in subsection 23(1) of the Oceans Act`
    `s 477.4(3)(b) a certificate issued by or under the authority of the Minister of Foreign Affairs`
    `s 477.4(3) a certificate of another kind`

@ref s 477.4(3) (src:8628-8632)
DECLARE `s 477.4(3) facts of the certificate` HAS
    `the kind of certificate`   IS A `s 477.4(3) the kind of certificate`
    `it contains a statement that a geographical location specified in it was, at a time material to the proceedings, in an area of a fishing zone of Canada that is not within the internal waters of Canada or the territorial sea of Canada`   IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)
    `it contains a statement that a geographical location specified in it was, at a time material to the proceedings, outside the territory of any state`   IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)

@ref s 477.4(3) (src:8628-8632)
GIVEN certificate IS A `s 477.4(3) facts of the certificate`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 477.4(3) the certificate is one referred to in subsection (3)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF certificate's `the kind of certificate` EQUALS `s 477.4(3)(a) a certificate referred to in subsection 23(1) of the Oceans Act` THEN JUST TRUE   -- (a)
        IF certificate's `the kind of certificate` EQUALS `s 477.4(3)(b) a certificate issued by or under the authority of the Minister of Foreign Affairs`
            THEN IF    certificate's `it contains a statement that a geographical location specified in it was, at a time material to the proceedings, in an area of a fishing zone of Canada that is not within the internal waters of Canada or the territorial sea of Canada`
                    OR certificate's `it contains a statement that a geographical location specified in it was, at a time material to the proceedings, outside the territory of any state`
                 THEN JUST TRUE   -- (b)
                 ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "containing a statement that any geographical location specified in the certificate was, at any time material to the proceedings, in an area of a fishing zone of Canada"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection names two kinds of certificate and says nothing of any other

@ref s 477.4(3) (src:8628-8632)
GIVEN `the certificate is one referred to in subsection (3), by s 477.4(3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are in respect of an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 477.4(3) the certificate is conclusive proof of the truth of the statement without proof of the signature or official character of the person appearing to have issued it` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the proceedings are in respect of an offence` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In proceedings in respect of an offence"
        IF `the certificate is one referred to in subsection (3), by s 477.4(3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(a) a certificate referred to in subsection 23(1) of the Oceans Act, or (b) a certificate issued by or under the authority of the Minister of Foreign Affairs" (a certificate not within them, or not determined)

-- src:8633 | Certificate cannot be compelled
-- src:8634 | (4) A certificate referred to in subsection (3) is admissible in evidence in proceedings referred to in that subsection but its production cannot be compelled.
@ref s 477.4(4) (src:8633-8634)
GIVEN `the certificate is one referred to in subsection (3), by s 477.4(3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are in respect of an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 477.4(4) the certificate is admissible in evidence in the proceedings` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the proceedings are in respect of an offence` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in proceedings referred to in that subsection"
        IF `the certificate is one referred to in subsection (3), by s 477.4(3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A certificate referred to in subsection (3)"

@ref s 477.4(4) (src:8633-8634)
GIVEN `the certificate is one referred to in subsection (3), by s 477.4(3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 477.4(4) the production of the certificate cannot be compelled` MEANS
    IF `the certificate is one referred to in subsection (3), by s 477.4(3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A certificate referred to in subsection (3)"
